WEBVTT

00:00:05.833 --> 00:00:07.333
Oh...

00:00:07.458 --> 00:00:09.833
Please excuse me, Mr Hunter.

00:00:09.958 --> 00:00:13.500
It seems I sat on the Spiky Red One.

00:00:13.625 --> 00:00:15.125
(Distant roaring)

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:20.083
What was that?

00:00:22.666 --> 00:00:25.916
(Aunt Lucy) 'If you ever get lost again...

00:00:26.041 --> 00:00:30.791
(Aunt Lucy and Paddington)
'...just roar and I'll roar right back.'

00:00:32.625 --> 00:00:34.041
(Roars)

00:00:37.875 --> 00:00:40.125
(Distant roaring)

00:00:40.791 --> 00:00:43.583
Aunt Lucy! She can hear me!

00:00:43.708 --> 00:00:45.958
That's how we find her, Mr Hunter.

00:00:46.083 --> 00:00:48.541
Like she always said.

00:00:48.666 --> 00:00:50.208
Follow her roars.

00:00:50.333 --> 00:00:51.833
(Thunder rumbling)

00:00:51.958 --> 00:00:53.416
(Thunderclap)

00:00:53.541 --> 00:00:55.375
(Door creaking)

00:01:27.583 --> 00:01:28.916
(Bell dings)

00:01:34.875 --> 00:01:36.541
(Beeping)

00:01:36.666 --> 00:01:38.916
What in God's name...?

00:01:39.041 --> 00:01:40.500
Language, Mrs Bird!

00:01:40.625 --> 00:01:45.791
What... Beg your pardon, Reverend Mother,
but this place...

00:01:45.916 --> 00:01:48.791
It looks kind of like an evil lair.

00:01:48.916 --> 00:01:51.250
- Oh, I can assure you it's not.
- (Whirring)

00:01:51.833 --> 00:01:53.666
(Mrs Bird muttering)

00:01:56.291 --> 00:01:58.833
But... Then, what is it?

00:01:58.958 --> 00:02:04.541
What it is, is a perfectly innocent
secret surveillance control centre.

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:08.000
And why on earth
would you need one of those?

00:02:08.916 --> 00:02:11.833
I confess, Mrs Bird, I have sinned!

00:02:11.958 --> 00:02:15.000
I have been deceitful
in a way most unbecoming of a nun,

00:02:15.125 --> 00:02:17.250
and I can only pray
for your forgiveness!

00:02:17.791 --> 00:02:18.791
What have you done?

00:02:19.625 --> 00:02:23.958
The St Christopher medal I gave Mary
is actually a secret tracking device.

00:02:24.083 --> 00:02:26.833
I couldn't let what happened
to poor Aunt Lucy happen again,

00:02:26.958 --> 00:02:28.875
so I've been keeping an eye
on them.

00:02:34.541 --> 00:02:36.250
Oh, my!

00:02:37.416 --> 00:02:39.416
That's a canny bit of kit!

00:02:40.041 --> 00:02:41.875
Someone's been a busy nun.

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:44.333
Well, thank goodness I have.
You see, this is Rumi Rock...

00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:48.000
...and this is the Browns' route.

00:02:48.125 --> 00:02:49.458
And they were heading
in the right direction,

00:02:49.583 --> 00:02:53.875
but now they're heading north
into uncharted, dangerous jungle,

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:56.125
and I fear for their safety.

00:02:56.791 --> 00:02:58.125
I'll alert the authorities.

00:02:58.250 --> 00:02:59.875
We'll mount a rescue party!

00:03:00.541 --> 00:03:03.666
No! Because they'll be too slow.
(Chuckles nervously)

00:03:03.791 --> 00:03:05.833
We must go ourselves.

00:03:05.958 --> 00:03:09.625
I thought you didnae go
trekking in the jungle?

00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:12.916
I thought it gave ye
the heebie-jeebies.

00:03:14.916 --> 00:03:16.875
I wasn't planning on trekking.

00:03:29.791 --> 00:03:30.875
Mary!

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:33.083
Not with the kids around.

00:03:38.333 --> 00:03:40.500
- (Screaming)
- Shh!

00:03:41.583 --> 00:03:43.750
There's something big out there.

00:03:46.166 --> 00:03:47.166
Hello?

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:53.083
Whatever you are...

00:03:54.458 --> 00:03:56.583
...you should know...

00:03:57.875 --> 00:04:00.666
...that I've got a twig here,

00:04:01.666 --> 00:04:04.291
...and I am not afraid to use it.

00:04:05.375 --> 00:04:07.208
(Leaves rustling)

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:14.375
(Screaming)

00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:16.041
Mary!

00:04:16.875 --> 00:04:18.166
- (Leaves rustling)
- (Thud)

00:04:18.291 --> 00:04:19.875
- (Gina) Ow!
- (Mrs Brown) Oh! Oh, no!

00:04:20.541 --> 00:04:23.458
Oh, Gina, I am so sorry.

00:04:23.583 --> 00:04:26.916
I... I thought you were some sort
of a fierce creature or something like...

00:04:27.041 --> 00:04:28.625
<i>¡Hola, Browns!</i>

00:04:28.750 --> 00:04:31.333
<i>¡Gracias a Dios!</i>
You're OK.

00:04:31.458 --> 00:04:33.416
Pretty pleased to see you, too.

00:04:33.541 --> 00:04:37.208
It was very clever using Jonathan's
deodorant spray as an odour trail.

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:40.416
Oh, yeah, I mean... that was the idea.

00:04:40.541 --> 00:04:41.583
Where did you get to?

00:04:41.708 --> 00:04:44.166
You and your father abandoned us
on an abandoned ship!

00:04:44.291 --> 00:04:45.916
- It wasn't abandoned.
- Yes, it was.

00:04:46.041 --> 00:04:47.333
It was only abandoned
after we abandoned it.

00:04:47.458 --> 00:04:49.458
Where is your tattooed father?

00:04:49.583 --> 00:04:52.125
There is something about him...

00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:53.666
I knew it.

00:04:53.791 --> 00:04:55.541
...about us...

00:04:56.625 --> 00:04:59.583
...that I should've told you
from the very beginning.

00:05:03.666 --> 00:05:07.125
My family are cursed
with a dreadful disease.

00:05:08.125 --> 00:05:12.791
They call it <i>el oro loco,</i>
gold madness.

00:05:12.916 --> 00:05:15.833
It began with my ancestor,
Gonzalo Caboto.

00:05:17.208 --> 00:05:19.416
'He was greedy and ruthless,

00:05:19.541 --> 00:05:22.166
'and when he heard
the legend of El Dorado,

00:05:22.291 --> 00:05:26.250
'he came looking for it,
driving his men to exhaustion.

00:05:28.041 --> 00:05:31.125
'He ate what he had to,
to stay alive,

00:05:31.250 --> 00:05:32.500
'but it was pointless.

00:05:33.208 --> 00:05:34.416
'Instead of riches,

00:05:34.541 --> 00:05:38.375
'all he passed onto his descendants
was greed.'

00:05:38.500 --> 00:05:40.541
(Evil chuckle)

00:05:40.666 --> 00:05:42.291
Huh? Oh!

00:05:43.416 --> 00:05:48.666
(Gina) 'Generation after generation,
fools in their pursuit of El Dorado.'

00:05:48.791 --> 00:05:50.333
- (Thud)
- Crikey!

00:05:51.541 --> 00:05:54.875
(Gina) 'Gold fever drew them
from every corner of the globe.'

